      "message": "The 2.5D `asM33()` change across the three text `RenderStep`s and `text_vertex_fn` makes sense and lines up with `VertexFiller::boundsAndDeviceMatrix` (where `sk_Position.w \u003d position.w` already carries the device-space `w` for perspective varying interpolation).\n\nOne test coverage note on `persptext_shader` in `gm/persptext.cpp`: because `SubRunControl::isSDFT` returns true for perspective outline text and the font uses `kAntiAlias`, `persptext_shader` exercises `SDFTextRenderStep` only. Would it be worth also exercising `SDFTextLCDRenderStep` (e.g. `kSubpixelAntiAlias` when the target surface has LCD pixel geometry) and `BitmapTextRenderStep` (e.g. an `kA8` bitmap glyph from `SkCustomTypefaceBuilder`, or a `Slug` recorded at identity and drawn under perspective) in the GM or a `DEF_GRAPHITE_TEST_FOR_RENDERING_CONTEXTS` pixel test?",
